!Sample_data_processing = Identification of significant clusters was performed via the standard FindClusters()algorithm in the Seurat package with a resolution parameter of 0.4 for PBMCs and 0.6 for brain. The cell type of each significant cluster was identified using marker genes generated by the Seurat function FindAllMarkers(). Major cell types were identified using formerly established cell markers in the literature (McManaman et al. 2013, Cho et al. 2017; Qian et al. 2017, Tillander et al. 2017; Heden et al. 2023, (Gropler et al. 2009; van Harmelen et al. 2007; Chen et al. 2015; VandeKopple et al. 2019; Maier et al. 2017; van Dierendonck et al. 2020; de la Rosa Rodriguez et al. 2021; Pulido et al. 2011; Dejgaard and Presley 2019; Zhang et al. 2024; Kiss and Nilsson 2014; Chen and Farese 2005; Chitraju et al. 2019; Chen 2006; Chitraju et al. 2017; Castoldi et al. 2020; Yen et al. 2008; Uchańska et al. 2024, CellMarker.2.0). One PBMC cluster was removed as identified contaminating red blood cells and three brain clusters were removed as unidentifiable clusters. The UMAPs within each cluster and condition were generated using ggplot2 (v. 3.4.4). Cell counts were found once the clusters were subset by condition.
